The terms of reference have been developed on the following initiatives: 
-	research the insurance systems in Uzbekistan and the best world practices and development of recommendations for improving the insurance system in agriculture and promoting the introduction of an effective crop insurance mechanisms:
-	Optimization of rice production systems towards water saving;
-	Creating favorable legal, institutional and financial environment for increasing the productive capacity of local farmers and dekhkans;
-	creation of MTB, alternative financial mechanisms, tax incentives for green technologies;
-	Assessing the needs of farmers and dekhkan farms in pilot districts;

Evaluation of the proposals is under process for development of technical solutions for the introduction of resource-saving irrigation systems to improve the efficiency of water resources utilization in the pilot districts
[2] experimental and demonstration plots of 2 ha were established in Kanlikul and Kegeyli districts to test and identify new promising varieties of winter cereals for the Aral Sea region;
[2] pilot plots were established to test winter garlic crops with high export potential in pilot areas in order to improve the knowledge and skills of dehkans and farmers in the production of high-yield crops;
[8] dehkans/farmers (2 women) and [3] representatives of the partner organization to increase participants knowledge in the production of highly profitable crops such as garlic, grapes, lemon and pistachio through field workshops through the study tour organized to Andijan and Ferghana regions in order to create a network for sharing knowledge and studying best practices in high-yield crop production between dekhkans and farmers from other regions of Uzbekistan. 

Brief analysis of the state of the agricultural sector in Kanlikul, Karauzyak and Kegeyli districts were developed and respective recommendations were prepared for facilitation of the process of developing the export potential of local farmers/dekhkans;

Conducted assessment and developed recommendations for improving the export potential of local agricultural producers/farmers in the pilot districts;

Currently the research works on the following tasks are in process: 
-	study and develop recommendations to increase the export potential of farms/dekhkan farms and increase the efficiency of exports of fruits and vegetables in pilot districts.
-	study of national legislation for compliance with international standards in the field of food safety and good agricultural practices such as Global GAP, HACCP, FSC, etc. Based on the results of the analysis and prepared recommendations, to assist farmers/entrepreneurs in the implementation of international standards for entering the Russian market, as well as the markets of other countries for local exports.

In order to improve social infrastructure and ensure access of rural communities to basic social services, community mobilization and needs assessments were conducted in the pilot districts and [6] CDPs were developed to further improve social infrastructure, including rehabilitation and improvement of social and local educational institutions
[2] water projects on reconstruction of water purifying station and construction of water-supply pipeline network are implemented in 2 pilot districts. The construction works are expected to complete by 1st quarter of 2023 and as result 2660 rural population will have access to clean drinking water.
